# tela/proof/extension-forms/src/forms.fab — formslib — the forms component
# family (the Stage 4 independent-extension proof, provider `formslib`).
#
# Stage 4 U2 (component-family — the static half). A SEPARATE package from
# the kernel (own faber.toml, own provider identity `formslib`, imported
# through the benchmark library-home machinery). The identity freeze +
# authoring constraints come from the U1 discovery record
# (stage-4-discovery.md).
#
# The family (four surface groups per the delivery U2 done_when (b)):
#   field (text input)    — campum / Props_campi   → form-field-<nomen>
#   checkbox              — boxum / Props_boxi     → form-checkbox-<nomen>
#   select                — selego / Props_selecti → form-select-<nomen>
#   error/live-region association — error_regionum (→ form-error-<nomen>,
#     the identity a field's aria-describedby references) + regio_viva_forma
#     (the form-level live region, form-live) + agmen_campi (the field
#     group: field + error node under form-control-<nomen>).
# The keyboard/validation structure is DECLARED here: the field/checkbox/
# select are natively focusable (native field semantics — Tab reaches them
# directly, the campaign §8 keyboard contract); the form-level
# focus-move/validation behavior belongs to the app-typed plan (U4).
#
# G4 consumability record (per export, the stage-1 §3 + U1 §4.2 evidence):
#   - The `→ tela.Visus` component fns (campum/selego/boxum/error_regionum/
#     regio_viva_forma/agmen_campi) reference the imported sibling type
#     tela.Visus in their signatures → WARN014 export-skipped for consumers
#     today (fix:g4). The package KEEPS its seam (never a duplicated Visus
#     in the package); the consumer's cross-package family composition stays
#     behind the documented compose-without workaround until g4 lands; the
#     gated U7 composes through normal qualified imports after the fix.
#   - The G4-safe surface stays on the exported file interface: the props
#     constructors (→ local classes — the Scopulus precedent, consumable)
#     and the `_html` string-returning render helpers (→ string — the U1
#     probe finding: the exempla asserts byte-exact through these, since the
#     exempla cannot consume the `→ tela.Visus` component fns through the
#     provider interface).
#   - Cross-package consumption (probed, U2 close): `forms.campum_html(
#     forms.props_campi(...))` (direct call result as an argument) and
#     `forms.props_campi(...).nomen` (field access on the call result)
#     resolve from a consumer; binding the constructor result to a `const`
#     with inferred type hits the provider-interface inference gap
#     (PARSE001 — the recorded G4/dialect family). The consumer composes
#     with the direct-call pattern until g4 lands.
#
# fix:<id> markers:
#   fix:g4 — the union-returning component exports are WARN014-skipped for
#     consumers (recorded above); removal = grep-replace after cds-u6
#     (file-interface-exports) lands; the gated U7 removes the workaround.
#   fix:g5 — NONE: campum/boxum/selego/error_regionum/regio_viva_forma/
#     agmen_campi/props_campi/props_boxi/props_selecti/*_html probed
#     collision-free on in-tree radix 0.80.0 (a free fn may share a class
#     name — G5's collision is enum-member-specific).
#   fix:snapshot-nomen-collision — the props classes (Props_campi/
#     Props_selecti/Props_boxi) avoid kernel type names (Spatium/Stilum/
#     Scopulum/Thema/Eventum/Effectus/Renovatio/Visus/…) AND the canary-app's
#     plan type names (Props_controlli/Vinculum/Nuntius — the app-typed plan
#     in U3/U4 lives app-side; the forms package keeps distinct names).
#   fix:codegen001 — Rust emit-across-imports persists (the TS lane is the
#     proven lane; recorded, never the gate).
#   fix:sem001 — HELD (U4): consumers read effect keys through
#     tela.effectus_identitas, never matching an imported union (the
#     G3-family imported-union match does not bind from a consumer); the
#     app-typed plan owns its message union, which is app-local.
#
# Stage 4 U4 (behavior-semantics) — the behavior contract + the pure
# validation-mapping surface. The components' documented
# event/identity/validation contract (below) is the semantics the
# consumer's plan relies on (the app-typed proof lives app-side in
# canary-app/src/main.fab — the D1 app-typed boundary, recorded). The
# SHARED-SOURCE statement: the same components that render statically in
# U2 carry the behavior contract; the interactive execution is U7 (gated —
# the dom-shim is not the interactive claim).
#
# The behavior contract (per component — the event surface, the identity
# scheme, the ARIA/validation semantics):
#   field (text input)  — identity form-field-<nomen>; events: "input"
#     (each text entry — the live-validation event) + "click" (pointer
#     activation on the native input); validation: aria-invalid
#     "true"/"false" + aria-describedby → form-error-<nomen> when invalid;
#     the error text lives in the associated error node (the agmen_campi
#     association, U2).
#   checkbox            — identity form-checkbox-<nomen>; events: "change"
#     (toggle) + "click"; aria-checked "true"/"false" + the invalid
#     surface (aria-invalid + aria-describedby → form-error-<nomen>).
#   select              — identity form-select-<nomen>; events: "change"
#     (selection change) + "click"; the invalid surface (aria-invalid +
#     aria-describedby → form-error-<nomen>).
#   form-level submit   — event "submit": the family declares the stable
#     spelling (eventus_submissionis); the U2 static surface renders no
#     <form> element, so the submit source is the app-declared form
#     aggregate — the app-typed plan owns it (D1: the concrete plan is the
#     application's surface, never kernel-generic).
#   live region         — identity form-live; role=status +
#     aria-live=polite; the announcement policy: announce on a
#     validation-state change, silent on no-op (the Stage 3 §1.5 pattern
#     extended to form validation) — carried by the app-typed plan.
# The event-name constants + the validation-state mapping fns (the U4
# surface at the end of this module) are pure string/bool signatures —
# G4-safe (they stay on the exported file interface; the consumer's plan
# builds on them without the WARN014 family). fix:g5 — the new identifiers
# (eventus_campi/eventus_mutationis/eventus_submissionis/eventus_click/
# invalid_textus/error_praesens) probed collision-free on in-tree radix
# 0.80.0.

import from "tela:tela" public * ut tela

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Typed props (per-component state carriers — local classes, consumable).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The field (text input) props. `invalid` = "true"/"false" (aria-invalid);
# `error` = the error message ("" = none — the group renders an empty error
# node; aria-describedby → form-error-<nomen> when invalid).
class Props_campi {
    string nomen
    string label
    string valor
    string invalid
    string error
}

# The select props (option list; aria-invalid + aria-describedby surface).
class Props_selecti {
    string nomen
    string label
    list<string> optiones
    string invalid
}

# The checkbox props. `selectus` = "true"/"false" (aria-checked).
class Props_boxi {
    string nomen
    string label
    string selectus
    string invalid
}

# Kernel-owned constructors (G3 posture — ordinary functions over the same
# public values; local-class-returning → consumable by the consumer today).
fn props_campi(string nomen, string label, string valor, string invalid, string error) → Props_campi {
    return Props_campi { nomen = nomen, label = label, valor = valor, invalid = invalid, error = error }
}

fn props_selecti(string nomen, string label, list<string> optiones, string invalid) → Props_selecti {
    return Props_selecti { nomen = nomen, label = label, optiones = optiones, invalid = invalid }
}

fn props_boxi(string nomen, string label, string selectus, string invalid) → Props_boxi {
    return Props_boxi { nomen = nomen, label = label, selectus = selectus, invalid = invalid }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The field (text input) — form-field-<nomen>.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn campum(Props_campi props) → tela.Visus {
    var list<tela.Attributum> attributa ← vacua
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "type", valor = "text" })
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-label", valor = props.label })
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-invalid", valor = props.invalid })
    if props.invalid ≡ "true" {
        attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-describedby", valor = "form-error-" + props.nomen })
    }
    if not (props.valor ≡ "") {
        attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "value", valor = props.valor })
    }
    return tela.elementum_omne(
        tela.nova_identitas("form-field-" + props.nomen),
        tela.html_spatium(),
        "input",
        attributa,
        [],
        []
    )
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The checkbox — form-checkbox-<nomen> (aria-checked + the invalid surface).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn boxum(Props_boxi props) → tela.Visus {
    var list<tela.Attributum> attributa ← vacua
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "type", valor = "checkbox" })
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-label", valor = props.label })
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-checked", valor = props.selectus })
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-invalid", valor = props.invalid })
    if props.invalid ≡ "true" {
        attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-describedby", valor = "form-error-" + props.nomen })
    }
    return tela.elementum_omne(
        tela.nova_identitas("form-checkbox-" + props.nomen),
        tela.html_spatium(),
        "input",
        attributa,
        [],
        []
    )
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The select — form-select-<nomen> (native option children).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn selego(Props_selecti props) → tela.Visus {
    var list<tela.Attributum> attributa ← vacua
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-label", valor = props.label })
    attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-invalid", valor = props.invalid })
    if props.invalid ≡ "true" {
        attributa.appende(tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-describedby", valor = "form-error-" + props.nomen })
    }
    var list<tela.Visus> liberi ← vacua
    var int i ← 0
    while i < props.optiones.longitudo() {
        liberi.appende(tela.elementum_view(tela.html_spatium(), "option", [ tela.textus_view(props.optiones[i]) ]))
        i ← i + 1
    }
    return tela.elementum_omne(
        tela.nova_identitas("form-select-" + props.nomen),
        tela.html_spatium(),
        "select",
        attributa,
        [],
        liberi
    )
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The error / live-region association.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The error node for a field: role=alert + the identity the field's
# aria-describedby references (form-error-<nomen>). Empty text = empty node
# (the association structure is stable — the group always carries it).
fn error_regionum(string nomen, string textus) → tela.Visus {
    var list<tela.Visus> liberi ← vacua
    if not (textus ≡ "") {
        liberi.appende(tela.textus_view(textus))
    }
    return tela.elementum_omne(
        tela.nova_identitas("form-error-" + nomen),
        tela.html_spatium(),
        "div",
        [ tela.Attributum { nomen = "role", valor = "alert" } ],
        [],
        liberi
    )
}

# The form-level live region (the Stage 3 §1.5 pattern extended to forms):
# role=status + aria-live=polite, form-live. The announcement policy (on a
# validation-state change, silent on no-op) is the app-typed plan's (U4).
fn regio_viva_forma() → tela.Visus {
    return tela.elementum_omne(
        tela.nova_identitas("form-live"),
        tela.html_spatium(),
        "div",
        [
            tela.Attributum { nomen = "role", valor = "status" },
            tela.Attributum { nomen = "aria-live", valor = "polite" }
        ],
        [],
        []
    )
}

# The field group — the association surface: the field (aria-describedby →
# form-error-<nomen> when invalid) + its error node under form-control-<nomen>.
fn agmen_campi(Props_campi props) → tela.Visus {
    var list<tela.Visus> liberi ← vacua
    liberi.appende(campum(props))
    liberi.appende(error_regionum(props.nomen, props.error))
    return tela.elementum_omne(
        tela.nova_identitas("form-control-" + props.nomen),
        tela.html_spatium(),
        "div",
        [],
        [],
        liberi
    )
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# G4-safe render helpers (the U1 probe finding): the exempla asserts the
# byte-exact static render through these string-returning helpers, since
# the `→ tela.Visus` component fns are WARN014-skipped for consumers
# (fix:g4). Serializer emission order: attributa in author order, then
# data-tela. Deterministic bytes over author order.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn campum_html(Props_campi props) → string {
    const string markup ← tela.html_visus(campum(props)) coalesce ""
    return markup
}

fn boxum_html(Props_boxi props) → string {
    const string markup ← tela.html_visus(boxum(props)) coalesce ""
    return markup
}

fn selego_html(Props_selecti props) → string {
    const string markup ← tela.html_visus(selego(props)) coalesce ""
    return markup
}

fn error_regionum_html(string nomen, string textus) → string {
    const string markup ← tela.html_visus(error_regionum(nomen, textus)) coalesce ""
    return markup
}

fn regio_viva_forma_html() → string {
    const string markup ← tela.html_visus(regio_viva_forma()) coalesce ""
    return markup
}

fn agmen_campi_html(Props_campi props) → string {
    const string markup ← tela.html_visus(agmen_campi(props)) coalesce ""
    return markup
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 4 U3 — namespaced `form.*` theme tokens, the component style
# bundles, and the product-assembly input (the three-package cascade's
# formslib contribution).
#
# Token surface (delivery U3 done_when (a)): zero-arg accessors returning
# the local token-carrier class (the extension `Scopulus` precedent) —
# consumers read fields on the call result (`forms.form_field_invalid()
# .nomen`/`.valor`); never a nameable qualified type, never a widened
# kernel `Scopulum` record. Token rendering is the kernel's (`thema_css` →
# `--form-field-invalid`). `form.focus` is the focus-ring token.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The local token-carrier class (distinct from the kernel `Scopulum` and the
# extension's `Scopulus` — fix:snapshot-nomen-collision).
class Scopula_formae {
    string nomen
    string valor
}

fn form_field_invalid() → Scopula_formae {
    return Scopula_formae { nomen = "form.field.invalid", valor = "#dc2626" }
}

fn form_field_valid() → Scopula_formae {
    return Scopula_formae { nomen = "form.field.valid", valor = "#16a34a" }
}

fn form_focus() → Scopula_formae {
    return Scopula_formae { nomen = "form.focus", valor = "#2563eb" }
}

# The token collection (the package's assembly-input convenience — the
# consumer composes the theme via the individual accessors, the field-access
# pattern; the collection is the package's self-usable summary).
fn scopulae_formae() → list<Scopula_formae> {
    return [ form_field_invalid(), form_field_valid(), form_focus() ]
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The family's component style bundle (delivery U3 done_when (b)): rules
# keyed on the family's data-tela identities (the dynamic identities ride
# attribute-prefix selectors), referencing the `--form-*` tokens. The
# Stilum-returning signature is class-returning → consumable from the
# consumer today (the stage-1 §3 evidence: `→ tela.Stilum` resolves).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn form_stilum() → tela.Stilum {
    return tela.Stilum {
        regulae = [
            tela.Regula {
                selector = "[data-tela^='form-field-']",
                declarationes = [
                    tela.Declaratio { nomen = "border-bottom", valor = "2px solid var(--form-field-invalid)" },
                    tela.Declaratio { nomen = "color", valor = "var(--form-field-valid)" }
                ]
            },
            tela.Regula {
                selector = "[data-tela^='form-field-']:focus",
                declarationes = [
                    tela.Declaratio { nomen = "outline", valor = "2px solid var(--form-focus)" }
                ]
            },
            tela.Regula {
                selector = "[data-tela^='form-error-']",
                declarationes = [
                    tela.Declaratio { nomen = "color", valor = "var(--form-field-invalid)" },
                    tela.Declaratio { nomen = "font-size", valor = "0.875rem" }
                ]
            },
            tela.Regula {
                selector = "[data-tela='form-live']",
                declarationes = [
                    tela.Declaratio { nomen = "font-weight", valor = "600" },
                    tela.Declaratio { nomen = "color", valor = "var(--form-field-valid)" }
                ]
            },
            tela.Regula {
                selector = "[data-tela^='form-checkbox-']",
                declarationes = [
                    tela.Declaratio { nomen = "accent-color", valor = "var(--form-field-valid)" }
                ]
            }
        ]
    }
}

# The product-assembly input surface (delivery U3 done_when (c)): the
# package contributes its Stilum-returning bundle + its package identity
# (`formslib` — the app declares the ordo entry app-side). The consumer
# wraps it: `tela.codicillus("formslib", forms.form_stilum())`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 4 U4 — the behavior-semantics contract surface.
#
# The event-name constants: the documented event spellings the consumers'
# bindings key to (the app-typed plan consumes these accessors — never a
# magic string in the plan). Zero-arg string accessors (G4-safe — the
# Scopulus accessor precedent).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn eventus_campi() → string {
    return "input"
}

fn eventus_mutationis() → string {
    return "change"
}

fn eventus_submissionis() → string {
    return "submit"
}

fn eventus_click() → string {
    return "click"
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The validation-state mapping fns (pure string/bool signatures — G4-safe):
#   invalid_textus — the validation state → the aria-invalid string
#     ("true"/"false");
#   error_praesens — the error text → whether the field is invalid (a
#     non-empty error = invalid — the describedby association + the error
#     node are live).
# The app-typed plan's update/validation semantics build on these
# (invalid → aria-invalid + error text; valid → cleared; the no-op rule).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn invalid_textus(bool invalid) → string {
    if invalid then return "true"
    return "false"
}

fn error_praesens(string error) → bool {
    return not (error ≡ "")
}
